14|🟡 T2 .NET Framework & Core|.NET Archi.how_it_works:
```
.NET compilation and execution pipeline:

  C# Source (.cs)  F# Source (.fs)
       ↓ C# compiler (Roslyn)    ↓ F# compiler
  IL (Intermediate Language) = .dll or .exe (PE format)
  └── Assembly manifest (metadata: type info, references)
  └── IL bytecode (platform-neutral instructions)
       ↓ CLR loads assembly
  CLR / CoreCLR (open-source .NET runtime)
  ├── Class Loader: loads types on first use
  ├── JIT Compiler (RyuJIT): compiles IL → native x64/ARM code
  │   - Tier 0 JIT: fast compilation, unoptimised (startup speed)
  │   - Tier 1 JIT: optimised compilation for hot methods (throughput)
  ├── GC (Garbage Collector): manages managed heap
  ├── Exception handling: structured exception handling (SEH)
  ├── Thread pool: manages worker and I/O completion threads
  └── Security: type safety, code access security

  Native code executes on CPU
```

