```
JIT compilation tiers (Tiered Compilation, default .NET 3.0+):

  Method first called:
  └── Tier 0 JIT: fast, minimal optimisation (~10ms to JIT)
      └── Native code runs (fast startup, lower peak throughput)

  Method called N times (hot, default threshold: ~30 calls):
  └── Tier 1 JIT: full optimisation (inlining, loop unrolling, SIMD)
      └── Optimised native code replaces Tier 0 code
      └── JIT can inline small methods called in hot loops

Key JIT optimisations:
  - Method inlining: replaces call with callee body (removes call overhead)
  - Dead code elimination: if (false) { ... } removed
  - Constant folding: 2 * 3 → 6 at JIT time
  - Loop unrolling: small fixed loops expanded inline
  - SIMD vectorisation: .NET 6+ uses AVX2/SSE2 intrinsics for array ops
  - Register allocation: variables in CPU registers, not stack
```

