```
GC generational model:

  Allocation: new objects go to Gen 0
  Gen 0 collection (every ~few hundred KB): fast, < 1ms
    → Dead objects: reclaimed
    → Surviving objects: promoted to Gen 1

  Gen 1 collection (when Gen 1 is full): medium, < 5ms
    → Dead objects: reclaimed
    → Surviving objects: promoted to Gen 2

  Gen 2 collection (full GC): slow, 1ms - 200ms depending on heap size
    → All surviving objects traced
    → LOH swept (not compacted — fragmentation accumulates)

  LOH (Large Object Heap): objects > 85KB
    → Allocated directly (no Gen 0)
    → Collected with Gen 2
    → NOT compacted by default (GC.Collect(2, GCCollectionMode.Forced, true, true) to compact)
```

